Who are we?
Centro is an international product development company with over 15 years of expertise in web development, commercial design, affiliate, and online marketing. Our diverse and talented team operates across various countries, including the USA, Canada, Cyprus, Ukraine, Poland, Georgia, and more.
Our project is the original home of independent creators producing niche digital content.
What you’ll be working on:

• Apply Agile and Scrum principles in day-to-day work while planning and managing project timelines, releases, and rollouts;

• Research, evaluate, and validate new product ideas aligned with company OKRs and overall product strategy;

• Define clear, well-structured product requirements and communicate them effectively to the development team, including technical context and feedback;

• Collaborate with other Product Owners and stakeholders to manage dependencies, align priorities, and ensure smooth, timely feature delivery

• Maintain regular communication with stakeholders to set expectations, gather input, and address questions;

• Scope resources, prioritize backlog items, and define sprint goals while monitoring progress and removing blockers;

• Lead by example to foster a collaborative, autonomous team environment and drive accountability;

• Take ownership of problem-solving by driving solutions, implementing fixes, and ensuring task completion;

• Design and execute A/B tests, and monitor product usage to continuously optimize Creator tools;

• Stay up to date with industry trends and conduct competitive analysis across both niche and mainstream markets;

• Understand user flows by implementing tracking, building reports and dashboards, and continuously optimizing flows based on data insights;

• Understand and track stakeholder KPIs, communicate performance insights, and adapt messaging for different audiences.

About you:

• 5+ years of experience as a Product Owner or Product Manager in a web development environment, with strong hands-on experience using AI tools as part of day-to-day product management workflows.

• Strong product thinking with the ability to identify high-impact opportunities, prioritize effectively, and drive initiatives from discovery to validation;

• User-first mindset with a strong focus on customer behavior, and business impact;

• Proven ability to rapidly prototype product concepts using AI-powered tools, validate ideas with users and data, and iterate quickly based on feedback.

• Data-driven approach to decision-making, including experience with product analytics, experimentation, and performance measurement;

• Experience with subscription-based products is a strong advantage;

• Demonstrated ability to think strategically, identify market opportunities, and translate business objectives into product initiatives with measurable outcomes.

• Strong understanding of OKR frameworks; outcome-driven product development, experimentation frameworks, and modern product operating model

• Comfortable working in AI-first product development environments where prototypes, AI-generated specifications, and rapid experimentation are used to accelerate delivery.

• Solid technical understanding of modern development workflows, tools, and engineering concepts;

• Hands-on experience with AI tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, Lovable, v0, or similar AI-powered workflows;

• Ability to leverage AI tools to accelerate product discovery, documentation, analysis, experimentation, and execution;

• Skilled in writing clear, structured, and actionable product requirements optimized for both human collaboration and AI-assisted workflows;

• Strong analytical, communication, and stakeholder management skills;

• Highly adaptable, detail-oriented, and comfortable operating in rapidly evolving environments;

• Strong ownership mindset with the ability to influence, inspire, and motivate cross-functional teams;

